  "id": "Compound::DB06795 - Gene::768",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Mafenide may interact with Ca9, through a series of biochemical pathways. Mafenide binds to Ca7, a protein involved in the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide, and this interaction is linked to Ca9's participation in the same pathway. Similarly, Mafenide also binds to Ca7, which is associated with carbonate dehydratase activity, another process that is also linked to Ca9. These findings indicate that Mafenide may influence Ca9 through the regulation of Ca7, which in turn affects the metabolic processes of Ca9. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Mafenide in modulating Ca9's function, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
